  "question": {
    "text": "A totally reflecting small plane mirror placed horizontally faces a parallel beam of light as shown in the figure. The mass of the mirror is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>. Assume that there is no absorption in the lens and that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the light emitted by the source goes through the lens. The power of the source needs to support the weight of the mirror is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>×</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>watt</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is [take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]<br />\r<img src=\"assets\\qt0010_8cb636906cc2.jpeg\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "15",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><msup><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>'</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>200</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8216;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MW</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>'</mi></msup><mn>0.2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1500</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#8196;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>"
